1
00:01:09,855 --> 00:01:13,333
<i>♪ On a cold, rainy day ♪</i>

2
00:01:14,511 --> 00:01:19,443
[We Buy, Sell &amp; Repair]
<i>♪ Sit in an old-fashioned coffeehouse ♪</i>

3
00:01:20,789 --> 00:01:25,807
<i>♪ Over a glass of Doraji whiskey ♪</i>

4
00:01:25,807 --> 00:01:31,346
<i>♪ And listen to that rich saxophone ♪</i>

5
00:01:42,561 --> 00:01:44,272
See anything you like?

6
00:01:44,272 --> 00:01:45,679
Oh, yes.

7
00:01:45,679 --> 00:01:47,679
How much is this?

8
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:50,879
How much have you got?

9
00:01:50,879 --> 00:01:52,792
One second.

10
00:01:57,357 --> 00:01:59,117
Let's see...

11
00:01:59,757 --> 00:02:02,235
Give me a thousand won. It's yours.

12
00:02:02,235 --> 00:02:04,479
A thousand won? Seriously?

13
00:02:04,479 --> 00:02:06,388
Are you sure?

14
00:02:06,388 --> 00:02:07,930
Yeah.

15
00:02:15,701 --> 00:02:17,104
Thank you.

16
00:02:17,104 --> 00:02:20,109
Have fun shooting with it.

17
00:02:20,109 --> 00:02:21,879
And take good care of it.

18
00:02:21,879 --> 00:02:24,724
I will. Thank you so much!

19
00:02:24,724 --> 00:02:29,954
<i>♪ At my age, after all these years ♪</i>

20
00:02:29,954 --> 00:02:34,288
<i>♪ What sweetness could heartbreak hold? ♪</i>

21
00:02:34,288 --> 00:02:39,584
<i>♪ Still, there's an empty space ♪</i>

22
00:02:39,584 --> 00:02:44,079
<i>♪ Somewhere in my heart ♪</i>

23
00:02:44,079 --> 00:02:48,264
<i>♪ For all that I've lost ♪</i>

24
00:02:48,264 --> 00:02:49,427
[Episode 1]

25
00:03:01,977 --> 00:03:03,607
[2010 Haesol City
Superintendent's Cup Judo Tournament]

26
00:03:11,897 --> 00:03:14,791
- You got this!
- Go, Yoon Ha Ru!

27
00:03:15,460 --> 00:03:17,037
You too, Woo Jae!

28
00:03:17,037 --> 00:03:19,440
But Ha Ru, you better win!

29
00:03:47,542 --> 00:03:48,811
Start!

30
00:03:48,811 --> 00:03:50,636
[Boys' High School Division]
[Yoon Ha Ru, Haesol High School]

31
00:03:50,636 --> 00:03:52,944
- Go for it!
- Go!

32
00:03:52,944 --> 00:03:55,259
- You got this!
- Go, go!

33
00:03:57,401 --> 00:04:00,407
- Yoon Ha Ru!
- Yoon Ha Ru!

34
00:04:00,407 --> 00:04:02,475
- Yoon Ha Ru!
- Yoon Ha Ru!

35
00:04:04,667 --> 00:04:08,485
The world's best are going head-to-head
in the men's under-73-kilogram division

36
00:04:08,485 --> 00:04:10,382
here at the Arcadia judo competition.

37
00:04:10,382 --> 00:04:12,578
We're at Arcadia Arena in Japan.

38
00:04:12,578 --> 00:04:14,321
Korea's Yoon Ha Ru.

39
00:04:14,321 --> 00:04:18,561
He's up against Kenji Sato,
who's dominated this weight class.

40
00:04:18,561 --> 00:04:21,025
Ha Ru is down by a half point,

41
00:04:21,025 --> 00:04:24,062
so he needs a full point
to turn this match around.

42
00:04:24,062 --> 00:04:27,447
Sato has a half-point lead,
but he keeps attacking.

43
00:04:27,447 --> 00:04:29,153
- That's right.
- Come on!

44
00:04:32,833 --> 00:04:35,003
Ha Ru keeps getting caught by his attacks.

45
00:04:35,003 --> 00:04:35,853
Go for the lead leg!

46
00:04:35,853 --> 00:04:39,108
Sato has a half-point lead,
but he keeps attacking.

47
00:04:39,108 --> 00:04:41,512
That's right. And Yoon Ha Ru...

48
00:04:41,512 --> 00:04:43,205
- Shoulder throw...
- He goes for a shoulder throw!

49
00:04:43,205 --> 00:04:45,053
- That was close.
- He avoids it. Good!

50
00:04:45,053 --> 00:04:47,344
- He goes in for a throw!
- Yeah, Yoon Ha Ru...

51
00:04:47,344 --> 00:04:49,299
- Nice.
- Oh, but now...

52
00:04:49,299 --> 00:04:50,475
Ha Ru's underneath!

53
00:04:50,475 --> 00:04:51,587
He can't let Sato pin him...

54
00:04:51,587 --> 00:04:53,524
<i>Pinning is called!</i>

55
00:04:53,524 --> 00:04:54,618
<i>He has to get out!</i>

56
00:04:54,618 --> 00:04:56,688
Time is running out!
Yoon Ha Ru! He has to escape!

57
00:04:56,688 --> 00:04:58,710
- Yoon Ha Ru!
- He has to get out!

58
00:04:58,710 --> 00:05:00,247
Sato keeps pressing.

59
00:05:00,247 --> 00:05:01,083
- Yoon Ha Ru!
- Bridge...

60
00:05:01,083 --> 00:05:03,582
He's out! He escaped!

61
00:05:04,806 --> 00:05:07,240
- That was dangerous.
- It was!

62
00:05:08,366 --> 00:05:10,277
Stop!

63
00:05:10,277 --> 00:05:13,091
Stop is called, and they're reset.

64
00:05:13,091 --> 00:05:15,482
Ha Ru needs to watch the clock.

65
00:05:15,482 --> 00:05:18,089
Yes, he's racing against time now.

66
00:05:18,089 --> 00:05:21,583
There's not much time left.
He has to keep attacking.

67
00:05:21,583 --> 00:05:22,862
Exactly.

68
00:05:22,862 --> 00:05:24,112
He needs a full point.

69
00:05:24,112 --> 00:05:27,086
He has to think fast, react fast, and go in.

70
00:05:27,086 --> 00:05:30,296
He needs a full point to come back.
There's still time.

71
00:05:30,296 --> 00:05:30,991
Start!

72
00:05:30,991 --> 00:05:33,099
You can do it, Yoon Ha Ru!

73
00:05:33,099 --> 00:05:36,712
He needs to stay aggressive.

74
00:05:36,712 --> 00:05:37,823
Nice combination!

75
00:05:37,823 --> 00:05:39,176
He's still got plenty in the tank.

76
00:05:39,176 --> 00:05:40,746
Go! Yoon Ha Ru!

77
00:05:40,746 --> 00:05:42,732
Go for the lead leg!

78
00:05:42,732 --> 00:05:43,883
Ha Ru attacks!

79
00:05:43,883 --> 00:05:45,848
- No, watch the counter!
- Yoon Ha Ru!

80
00:05:45,848 --> 00:05:48,281
Now, can he...

81
00:05:58,032 --> 00:05:59,762
- He's done it!
- Nice!

82
00:05:59,762 --> 00:06:01,803
Yoon Ha Ru! Can you believe it?

83
00:06:01,803 --> 00:06:04,473
- Stop!
- Stop!

84
00:06:04,473 --> 00:06:05,644
A shoulder throw!

85
00:06:05,644 --> 00:06:07,328
Incredible! Korea's Yoon Ha Ru!

86
00:06:07,328 --> 00:06:10,675
He takes down the world's best, Kenji Sato!

87
00:06:10,675 --> 00:06:12,921
He was in a very tough spot just then.

88
00:06:12,921 --> 00:06:16,654
He went for a large outer reap,
and Sato tried to counter,

89
00:06:16,654 --> 00:06:18,980
but Ha Ru pulled his leg free
and transitioned into a shoulder throw.

90
00:06:18,980 --> 00:06:21,258
- What incredible focus!
- That was nice.

91
00:06:21,258 --> 00:06:22,788
He is unbelievable.

92
00:06:22,788 --> 00:06:24,133
- Amazing.
- Absolutely.

93
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:28,364
<i>Yoon Ha Ru defeats Kenji Sato
and takes gold for Korea!</i>

94
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:37,970
See? Ha Ru takes after me.
That's why he's so good!

95
00:06:37,970 --> 00:06:40,246
What are you talking about? He takes after me!

96
00:06:40,246 --> 00:06:42,477
[Judo Idol Yoon Ha Ru Wins Gold]
No! He takes after me!

97
00:06:42,477 --> 00:06:43,987
Quiet!

98
00:06:43,987 --> 00:06:47,324
With five seconds left,
you pulled off a dramatic shoulder throw.

99
00:06:47,324 --> 00:06:51,714
Everyone said beating Kenji Sato
would be impossible.

100
00:06:51,714 --> 00:06:53,978
I never thought it was impossible.

101
00:06:53,978 --> 00:06:56,751
I just felt like I was going to win.

102
00:06:56,751 --> 00:06:59,211
Did you have some kind of special feeling?

103
00:06:59,211 --> 00:07:01,449
Not a feeling, exactly...

104
00:07:01,449 --> 00:07:07,453
More like a special kind of faith and love.

105
00:07:07,453 --> 00:07:08,826
Actually...

106
00:07:08,826 --> 00:07:10,772
I'll be honest with you.

107
00:07:10,772 --> 00:07:12,610
Yes?

108
00:07:12,610 --> 00:07:16,229
More than when I threw Kenji Sato on that mat,

109
00:07:16,229 --> 00:07:20,828
seeing my fans from up here on the podium...

110
00:07:20,828 --> 00:07:23,480
makes my heart race even faster.

111
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:27,664
Now I see why they call you the idol of judo.

112
00:07:27,664 --> 00:07:32,131
Would you say a few words
to everyone in Korea and your fans?

113
00:07:32,131 --> 00:07:33,656
Of course.

114
00:07:35,079 --> 00:07:38,863
To everyone in Korea
who supported me through these tough times,

115
00:07:38,863 --> 00:07:43,001
<i>and to all my fans
who have always stood by me...</i>

116
00:07:43,001 --> 00:07:47,980
your love and support
put this gold medal around my neck.

117
00:07:47,980 --> 00:07:49,805
I love you all.

118
00:07:51,183 --> 00:07:57,520
Any words for actress Yoon Ha Na?
She must be thrilled for you.

119
00:07:58,959 --> 00:08:00,559
Yoon Ha Na?

120
00:08:04,371 --> 00:08:05,490
[A Hollow Craft, Stripped of Sincerity]

121
00:08:05,490 --> 00:08:09,874
"Yoon Ha Na once burned with life,
becoming each role.

122
00:08:09,874 --> 00:08:13,840
Now, where her own emotions have dried up,

123
00:08:14,970 --> 00:08:20,117
she fills the void with soulless imitation."

124
00:08:50,140 --> 00:08:53,447
Congratulations, Ms. Yoon.

125
00:08:54,659 --> 00:08:56,349
For what?

126
00:08:56,349 --> 00:08:57,750
Sorry?

127
00:08:57,750 --> 00:08:59,862
Oh, well...

128
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:03,744
Sorry. My mind was somewhere else.

129
00:09:03,744 --> 00:09:05,916
What were you congratulating me for?

130
00:09:05,916 --> 00:09:09,720
Yoon Ha Ru just won the gold medal.

131
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:12,757
Oh, really? Thank you.

132
00:09:12,757 --> 00:09:16,100
With both of you doing so well,
your parents must be thrilled.

133
00:09:16,100 --> 00:09:17,113
Not really.

134
00:09:17,113 --> 00:09:20,156
By tomorrow, Ha Ru's ego
will be through the roof,

135
00:09:20,156 --> 00:09:22,341
and he'll drive us all crazy.

136
00:09:22,341 --> 00:09:26,495
I already can't stand him.

137
00:09:26,495 --> 00:09:28,105
Have some rest.

138
00:09:32,273 --> 00:09:34,260
What's up?

139
00:09:34,260 --> 00:09:36,013
Did he win?

140
00:09:39,675 --> 00:09:42,157
I have nothing to say to her.

141
00:09:42,157 --> 00:09:43,834
She probably didn't even watch my match.

142
00:09:43,834 --> 00:09:46,974
She couldn't care less about me.
All she does is tell me to quit showing off.

143
00:09:46,974 --> 00:09:48,142
So, nothing.

144
00:09:48,142 --> 00:09:50,584
You two really don't hold back with each other.

145
00:09:50,584 --> 00:09:54,048
Any final words before we wrap up?

146
00:09:54,048 --> 00:09:56,048
Final words...

147
00:09:58,059 --> 00:10:01,138
Actually, there's someone I really love.

148
00:10:01,138 --> 00:10:03,711
<i>I'd like to say something to him.</i>

149
00:10:03,711 --> 00:10:07,360
<i>Someone you really love?</i>

150
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:09,862
<i>Now you've got me curious.</i>

151
00:10:09,862 --> 00:10:13,930
<i>He's a friend who's way better
at judo than I am.</i>

152
00:10:14,784 --> 00:10:16,039
[Judo Idol Yoon Ha Ru Wins Gold]

153
00:10:16,039 --> 00:10:18,121
<i>Hey, Jung Woo Jae!</i>

154
00:10:18,121 --> 00:10:19,867
<i>You watching?</i>

155
00:10:21,563 --> 00:10:23,637
<i>I kept my promise.</i>

156
00:10:25,497 --> 00:10:28,542
You did well, Yoon Ha Ru.

157
00:10:37,022 --> 00:10:40,592
There'll be even more reporters
than usual because of Ha Ru.

158
00:10:40,592 --> 00:10:42,722
Be on your game.

159
00:10:42,722 --> 00:10:44,536
I'm already doing enough.

160
00:10:44,536 --> 00:10:47,099
I was cheering on my twin even from overseas.

161
00:10:47,099 --> 00:10:50,700
I may look worn out,
but I should at least look happy.

162
00:10:50,700 --> 00:10:53,057
I need that close-sibling image.

163
00:10:53,057 --> 00:10:56,310
You're not selling it.

164
00:10:56,310 --> 00:10:58,334
Look at your face.

165
00:10:58,334 --> 00:11:01,210
Does that look like a happy face?

166
00:11:04,468 --> 00:11:09,142
You can fool reporters,
but you can't fool the camera.

167
00:11:09,142 --> 00:11:11,344
Oh, come on.

168
00:11:11,344 --> 00:11:15,857
I'm just prepping for my next role.
She's got a tragic past.

169
00:11:15,857 --> 00:11:17,227
Look at my eyes.

170
00:11:17,227 --> 00:11:19,148
More soulful, right?

171
00:11:19,148 --> 00:11:20,641
Yoon Ha Na.

172
00:11:20,641 --> 00:11:22,098
Yeah, CEO Seo Ye Rang.

173
00:11:22,098 --> 00:11:23,548
- You...
- Okay, okay.

174
00:11:23,548 --> 00:11:25,065
Stop worrying.

175
00:11:25,065 --> 00:11:26,282
You know who I am, right?

176
00:11:26,282 --> 00:11:28,330
I'm Yoon Ha Na.

177
00:11:29,118 --> 00:11:30,971
You're impossible.

178
00:11:40,941 --> 00:11:42,519
What's taking her so long?

179
00:11:42,519 --> 00:11:44,512
Ha Na.

180
00:11:44,512 --> 00:11:46,036
I want to see her already!

181
00:11:46,036 --> 00:11:47,513
When is she coming out?

182
00:11:47,513 --> 00:11:49,213
She's taking forever.

183
00:11:49,213 --> 00:11:51,354
I want to see her.

184
00:11:53,206 --> 00:11:54,631
Ha Na!

185
00:11:54,631 --> 00:11:55,768
She's here.

186
00:11:55,768 --> 00:11:57,063
All teams, hold formation.

187
00:11:57,063 --> 00:11:58,717
Moving out.

188
00:11:59,598 --> 00:12:01,084
Take it slow.

189
00:12:01,084 --> 00:12:02,899
- This way, please.
- Ha Na!

190
00:12:05,057 --> 00:12:06,268
One moment!

191
00:12:06,268 --> 00:12:09,280
As his twin, did you have
a feeling he would win?

192
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:11,239
Any words for Yoon Ha Ru?

193
00:12:11,239 --> 00:12:15,009
Not really. I just knew he'd do well.

194
00:12:15,009 --> 00:12:16,715
Congrats, Ha Ru.

195
00:12:18,015 --> 00:12:20,295
- Did you expect him to win?
- Ha Na!

196
00:12:20,295 --> 00:12:21,995
Step back, please!

197
00:12:28,554 --> 00:12:29,657
The teddy bear's eye...

198
00:12:29,657 --> 00:12:31,390
What is that?

199
00:12:31,390 --> 00:12:33,692
Are you okay?

200
00:12:33,692 --> 00:12:36,131
- Who sent this?
- Ha Na! Are you okay?

201
00:12:36,131 --> 00:12:38,891
<i>You can't even cry!</i>

202
00:12:41,043 --> 00:12:44,240
<i>You can't even cry!</i>

203
00:12:45,986 --> 00:12:49,099
<i>You can't even cry!</i>

204
00:12:52,493 --> 00:12:54,699
Ha Na.

205
00:12:54,699 --> 00:12:57,153
We're on camera right now.

206
00:13:09,487 --> 00:13:10,945
Excuse me.

207
00:13:10,945 --> 00:13:12,221
Excuse me.

208
00:13:12,221 --> 00:13:15,105
- Ha Na!
- Ha Na!

209
00:13:37,375 --> 00:13:39,985
What the hell are the police doing?

210
00:13:39,985 --> 00:13:43,495
Put him under surveillance.
Form a task force. Do something!

211
00:13:43,495 --> 00:13:48,980
How have they failed to stop
or catch that rat for years?

212
00:13:48,980 --> 00:13:50,313
Screw procedure.

213
00:13:50,313 --> 00:13:52,830
I want an update on the investigation by...

214
00:13:52,830 --> 00:13:55,109
[Six Months Earlier]

215
00:13:56,477 --> 00:13:59,017
<i>- Emotional numbness?
- Yes.</i>

216
00:13:59,017 --> 00:14:05,617
<i>Your brain is slower to register
what you're feeling, even joy or sadness.</i>

217
00:14:05,617 --> 00:14:06,969
<i>Why me...</i>

218
00:14:06,969 --> 00:14:11,975
<i>It can happen to people like you,
who constantly manage their emotions.</i>

219
00:14:11,975 --> 00:14:14,574
<i>The mind can get overloaded too.</i>

220
00:14:14,574 --> 00:14:17,565
<i>But it shouldn't affect
your day-to-day life much.</i>

221
00:14:17,565 --> 00:14:22,226
<i>Could it affect my acting?</i>

222
00:14:22,226 --> 00:14:23,716
<i>It's possible.</i>

223
00:14:23,716 --> 00:14:26,804
<i>It impairs your ability
to feel and express emotions.</i>

224
00:14:30,306 --> 00:14:32,759
Get that in writing.

225
00:14:35,018 --> 00:14:37,386
Hello, Reporter Kim?

226
00:14:39,425 --> 00:14:41,998
I think it was around here.

227
00:14:47,043 --> 00:14:48,744
This guy.

228
00:14:52,081 --> 00:14:54,814
Can you zoom in from a better angle?

229
00:14:56,147 --> 00:14:58,490
The image is too pixelated...

230
00:14:59,694 --> 00:15:02,685
Is that a scar?

231
00:15:02,685 --> 00:15:04,186
Hard to tell.

232
00:17:01,077 --> 00:17:03,527
Why'd you turn the lights off?

233
00:17:03,527 --> 00:17:05,787
I need to take my makeup off.

234
00:17:05,787 --> 00:17:07,337
Then get up.

235
00:17:07,337 --> 00:17:09,385
I have no energy.

236
00:17:09,385 --> 00:17:12,711
I can't even lift a finger.

237
00:17:14,444 --> 00:17:16,955
I'm not washing your face for you.

238
00:17:18,603 --> 00:17:23,058
You think just anyone gets to touch my face?

239
00:17:24,054 --> 00:17:25,824
We're leaving at 11 tomorrow, right?

240
00:17:25,824 --> 00:17:27,354
Wash up and get some sleep.

241
00:17:27,354 --> 00:17:28,899
I'm leaving.

242
00:17:29,630 --> 00:17:31,690
Take my makeup off for me.

243
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:36,360
Just for tonight.

244
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:39,140
I have a dress fitting tomorrow.

245
00:17:40,519 --> 00:17:43,269
Just this once.

246
00:17:43,269 --> 00:17:44,723
Please?

247
00:18:44,663 --> 00:18:46,179
Oh, right.

248
00:18:46,179 --> 00:18:49,744
That camcorder's still
in the living room cabinet.

249
00:18:49,744 --> 00:18:51,467
Oh, yeah.

250
00:18:51,467 --> 00:18:53,727
It doesn't even turn on anymore.

251
00:18:55,360 --> 00:18:56,597
You should've had it fixed.

252
00:18:56,597 --> 00:18:58,787
It was already junk when I bought it.

253
00:18:58,787 --> 00:19:00,984
It's probably beyond repair.

254
00:19:05,136 --> 00:19:07,148
Don't you ever get tired of it?

255
00:19:08,216 --> 00:19:09,288
Of what?

256
00:19:09,288 --> 00:19:11,789
Being around me.

257
00:19:11,789 --> 00:19:13,377
Being my friend.

258
00:19:16,084 --> 00:19:19,677
You don't exactly give me time to get bored.

259
00:19:19,677 --> 00:19:22,181
True. You've got a point.

260
00:19:22,181 --> 00:19:24,850
I am pretty irresistible.

261
00:19:26,886 --> 00:19:28,562
Did you take your meds?

262
00:19:30,780 --> 00:19:32,112
Yeah.

263
00:19:32,112 --> 00:19:34,311
Getting sleepy?

264
00:19:34,311 --> 00:19:36,224
I think so.

265
00:19:37,731 --> 00:19:39,815
Want me to put a face mask on you?

266
00:19:39,815 --> 00:19:41,333
Yeah.

267
00:19:52,740 --> 00:19:56,115
[No Caller ID]

268
00:20:14,267 --> 00:20:15,439
<i>Congrats on the gold!</i>

269
00:20:15,439 --> 00:20:18,042
<i>- You're back, huh? Let's grab a drink!
- You were amazing!</i>

270
00:20:18,042 --> 00:20:19,507
<i>Let's meet up soon.</i>

271
00:20:20,900 --> 00:20:22,771
<i>You landed, right?</i>

272
00:20:28,863 --> 00:20:31,422
[My Boss]

273
00:20:32,119 --> 00:20:33,954
Yeah, I just landed.

274
00:20:33,954 --> 00:20:34,992
Where are you?

275
00:20:34,992 --> 00:20:38,542
<i>Where else? In your heart, of course.</i>

276
00:20:38,542 --> 00:20:40,294
Not Jung Woo Jae's?

277
00:20:40,294 --> 00:20:43,368
<i>Why? What are you sulking about now?</i>

278
00:20:43,368 --> 00:20:46,650
You said you love him more than anyone.

279
00:20:46,650 --> 00:20:48,052
News to me.

280
00:20:48,052 --> 00:20:50,015
<i>Oh, babe.</i>

281
00:20:50,015 --> 00:20:52,625
<i>You seriously didn't know?</i>

282
00:20:53,432 --> 00:20:54,259
What?

283
00:20:54,259 --> 00:20:59,127
Of course I love Jung Woo Jae.
More than life itself.

284
00:20:59,823 --> 00:21:00,856
Then what about me?

285
00:21:00,856 --> 00:21:03,092
You're...

286
00:21:05,016 --> 00:21:09,448
You're my boss for life.

287
00:21:09,448 --> 00:21:11,448
- What?
<i>- You're the boss, so...</i>

288
00:21:11,448 --> 00:21:13,942
you're stuck leading me till I die.

289
00:21:13,942 --> 00:21:15,621
Seo Ye Rang.

290
00:21:15,621 --> 00:21:17,345
Lucky you.

291
00:21:17,345 --> 00:21:19,147
You're thrilled, right?

292
00:21:21,016 --> 00:21:25,445
Sorry, I'm really not
in the mood to be thrilled.

293
00:21:25,445 --> 00:21:27,265
Why? Something happen?

294
00:21:27,265 --> 00:21:28,789
Well...

295
00:21:28,789 --> 00:21:30,845
It's about Ha Na's article.

296
00:21:30,845 --> 00:21:32,251
Yoon Ha Na?

297
00:21:32,251 --> 00:21:34,471
What about her?

298
00:21:34,471 --> 00:21:36,695
Come on, look.

299
00:21:36,695 --> 00:21:38,538
How do I look? Normal?

300
00:21:38,538 --> 00:21:40,798
Like none of this got to me?

301
00:21:42,874 --> 00:21:44,481
How about this face?

302
00:21:47,411 --> 00:21:50,363
That's your press conference face.

303
00:21:53,951 --> 00:21:55,737
Smile again.

304
00:22:03,645 --> 00:22:05,307
Got it. Toothpaste commercial?

305
00:22:05,307 --> 00:22:07,089
Stop messing around.

306
00:22:07,089 --> 00:22:10,203
Oh, that one. That looked the most natural.

307
00:22:10,203 --> 00:22:12,499
I'm not asking you anymore.

308
00:22:17,693 --> 00:22:19,977
Just pretend they're all me.

309
00:22:19,977 --> 00:22:21,963
Everyone out there.

310
00:22:23,061 --> 00:22:26,314
Just relax, like you are now.

311
00:22:29,701 --> 00:22:31,400
[Ha Na Smiles Brightly with Eyeless Doll]

312
00:22:34,368 --> 00:22:36,161
Hello.

313
00:22:36,161 --> 00:22:38,329
- Hello.
- Hello.

314
00:22:38,329 --> 00:22:39,341
Oh my!

315
00:22:39,341 --> 00:22:41,403
My sweetheart! You're here!

316
00:22:41,403 --> 00:22:43,553
- How have you been?
- Oh my.

317
00:22:43,553 --> 00:22:46,452
This is for you.
It's from the most famous patissier in Paris.

318
00:22:46,452 --> 00:22:49,924
- Oh my!
- The sugar work is so delicate...

319
00:22:49,924 --> 00:22:52,134
It reminded me of the beading on your dresses.

320
00:22:52,134 --> 00:22:53,233
My goodness!

321
00:22:53,233 --> 00:22:55,709
You didn't have to!

322
00:22:55,709 --> 00:22:57,537
I'm so touched.

323
00:22:57,537 --> 00:22:59,640
You're just too sweet. I adore you.

324
00:22:59,640 --> 00:23:00,601
Eun Jung, Ji Yoon.

325
00:23:00,601 --> 00:23:03,771
These are for you.
Have one when you need a sugar boost.

326
00:23:03,771 --> 00:23:05,815
Ji Yoon, you cut your bangs!

327
00:23:05,815 --> 00:23:07,691
They look so cute.

328
00:23:07,691 --> 00:23:09,777
You're always so thoughtful.

329
00:23:09,777 --> 00:23:11,325
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

330
00:23:11,325 --> 00:23:12,530
By the way...

331
00:23:12,530 --> 00:23:14,083
You saw the article, right?

332
00:23:15,024 --> 00:23:18,899
"Chucky and the Joker land
at Incheon Airport..."

333
00:23:18,899 --> 00:23:21,693
I need to look drop-dead gorgeous
at this awards show.

334
00:23:21,693 --> 00:23:24,250
No more Joker jokes.

335
00:23:24,250 --> 00:23:26,156
So what am I wearing?

336
00:23:26,156 --> 00:23:27,545
Leave it to me.

337
00:23:27,545 --> 00:23:28,659
Trust me.

338
00:23:28,659 --> 00:23:30,589
Come on, get in there.

339
00:23:30,589 --> 00:23:33,759
You look fabulous today!

340
00:23:33,759 --> 00:23:35,833
Welcome. Come on.

341
00:23:35,833 --> 00:23:38,097
I went with a G-Dragon look today.

342
00:23:38,097 --> 00:23:40,790
Ms. Yoon's fitting is done.

343
00:23:51,790 --> 00:23:55,960
Oh my god.

344
00:24:21,312 --> 00:24:23,392
Oh wow. Gorgeous.

345
00:24:23,392 --> 00:24:28,328
My dress looks even better on you.

346
00:24:31,042 --> 00:24:32,400
Hello.

347
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:33,734
Hey, what are you doing here?

348
00:24:33,734 --> 00:24:34,737
Hi.

349
00:24:34,737 --> 00:24:37,990
- What was with that photo yesterday?
- Oh, you're here.

350
00:24:37,990 --> 00:24:40,044
I called him.

351
00:24:42,298 --> 00:24:43,634
Oh, yeah.

352
00:24:43,634 --> 00:24:46,707
Right. Big brother came to see you.

353
00:24:46,707 --> 00:24:48,209
You think I'm here to try on dresses?

354
00:24:48,209 --> 00:24:52,097
Big brother, my foot.
You're only two minutes older.

355
00:24:52,097 --> 00:24:54,465
Two minutes is a huge difference.

356
00:24:54,465 --> 00:24:57,343
Why has it been so long since you've come by?

357
00:24:57,343 --> 00:25:00,709
Didn't Ha Na tell you how much I missed you?

358
00:25:00,709 --> 00:25:03,015
- She didn't.
- My goodness!

359
00:25:03,015 --> 00:25:05,392
Oh, wow! Look at that body.

360
00:25:05,392 --> 00:25:08,312
A work of art.

361
00:25:08,312 --> 00:25:12,483
Let me make you a killer suit
to celebrate that gold medal.

362
00:25:12,483 --> 00:25:15,371
I'm good, but I appreciate it.

363
00:25:15,371 --> 00:25:16,445
Don't just appreciate it.

364
00:25:16,445 --> 00:25:19,021
Take the gifts!

365
00:25:19,742 --> 00:25:22,189
Don't smile at me like that!

366
00:25:22,189 --> 00:25:25,926
You're making my heart race.

367
00:25:25,926 --> 00:25:27,873
So...

368
00:25:27,873 --> 00:25:30,334
- Shall we go with this one?
- Yes, this is the one!

369
00:25:30,334 --> 00:25:31,502
It's perfect.

370
00:25:31,502 --> 00:25:33,948
Absolutely beautiful!

371
00:25:34,958 --> 00:25:37,041
I'm making you something. No arguments.

372
00:25:37,041 --> 00:25:38,841
Really, I'm fine.

373
00:25:40,470 --> 00:25:41,797
What?

374
00:25:41,797 --> 00:25:43,681
Emotional what?

375
00:25:43,681 --> 00:25:46,476
My emotions are on strike.

376
00:25:46,476 --> 00:25:47,849
Is that an actual diagnosis?

377
00:25:47,849 --> 00:25:50,146
That's private medical information.

378
00:25:50,146 --> 00:25:52,357
You don't need the details.

379
00:25:52,357 --> 00:25:53,722
Just tell me what's going on.

380
00:25:53,722 --> 00:25:55,735
I did. That's exactly what it is.

381
00:25:55,735 --> 00:25:59,689
Funny things aren't funny,
and sad things don't make me sad.

382
00:25:59,689 --> 00:26:03,321
My emotions won't do their job,
so they're on strike.

383
00:26:05,110 --> 00:26:09,642
Babe, am I the only one confused?
What is she even saying?

384
00:26:09,642 --> 00:26:12,175
Just eat this.

385
00:26:16,046 --> 00:26:17,382
- Spicy, but good.
- Right?

386
00:26:17,382 --> 00:26:18,895
Yeah.

387
00:26:19,710 --> 00:26:21,302
So...

388
00:26:21,302 --> 00:26:25,140
she's saying she can't really
feel emotions right now?

389
00:26:25,140 --> 00:26:26,245
Yeah.

390
00:26:26,245 --> 00:26:29,602
For real? Even that nasty temper of hers?

391
00:26:29,602 --> 00:26:30,931
Enough.

392
00:26:30,931 --> 00:26:32,806
Yoon Ha Ru, stop.

393
00:26:37,166 --> 00:26:40,864
Watching you play sweet
for the cameras makes me gag.

394
00:26:40,864 --> 00:26:43,903
You had a runny nose till second grade,
and now you act like a goddess.

395
00:26:43,903 --> 00:26:48,448
You're two minutes younger
and somehow look older than me.

396
00:26:53,230 --> 00:26:55,295
Crispy and good.

397
00:26:55,295 --> 00:26:56,630
Oh my.

398
00:26:57,742 --> 00:26:58,996
Don't bother.

399
00:26:58,996 --> 00:27:02,973
I don't have a shred of emotion
or energy to waste on you.

400
00:27:02,973 --> 00:27:05,915
- No way...
- I need to sleep. I'm filming tomorrow.

401
00:27:05,915 --> 00:27:08,968
- Oh my dear, what happened...
- Don't be dramatic.

402
00:27:08,968 --> 00:27:11,025
Once I'm better,
you're the first one I'm killing.

403
00:27:11,025 --> 00:27:15,416
My emotions stopped working, not my brain.

404
00:27:22,504 --> 00:27:24,115
- David.
- "David?"

405
00:27:24,115 --> 00:27:27,035
This is the biggest surprise ever.

406
00:27:27,035 --> 00:27:29,204
- Can we talk in private?
- What? A guy?

407
00:27:29,204 --> 00:27:32,630
He directed "Lunard Crystal," you idiot.

408
00:27:35,502 --> 00:27:39,506
Your favorite director
that no one's ever heard of?

409
00:27:39,506 --> 00:27:42,050
He won the Grand Jury Prize
at Sundance this year.

410
00:27:42,050 --> 00:27:45,060
He's Hollywood's hottest
new director right now.

411
00:27:45,060 --> 00:27:46,221
Okay.

412
00:27:46,221 --> 00:27:49,512
- Hollywood?
- Oh my God.

413
00:27:49,512 --> 00:27:52,356
You really mean Ha Na?

414
00:27:52,356 --> 00:27:53,946
It's a casting offer.

415
00:27:53,946 --> 00:27:55,908
A casting offer!

416
00:27:56,877 --> 00:27:59,032
Absolutely.

417
00:27:59,032 --> 00:28:00,721
David.

418
00:28:00,721 --> 00:28:04,948
She read the script
and she was like, genuinely impressed.

419
00:28:04,948 --> 00:28:07,180
I'm tired. I'm going to bed.

420
00:28:09,065 --> 00:28:10,590
What?

421
00:28:10,590 --> 00:28:14,045
Her favorite director offered her a role,
and she didn't even brag?

422
00:28:14,045 --> 00:28:15,844
She didn't even jump for joy...

423
00:28:15,844 --> 00:28:17,620
Is this real life?

424
00:28:17,620 --> 00:28:19,483
- Open up.
- Okay.

425
00:28:22,801 --> 00:28:24,984
Spicy, but good.

426
00:28:29,259 --> 00:28:31,683
- Sorry, I have to leave early.
- It's okay.

427
00:28:31,683 --> 00:28:33,388
- Take good care of Ha Na.
- I will.

428
00:28:33,388 --> 00:28:35,184
- I'll call you.
- Okay.

429
00:28:35,184 --> 00:28:37,155
Love you.

430
00:28:37,155 --> 00:28:38,134
- I'm off.
- Okay.

431
00:28:38,134 --> 00:28:40,008
- See you.
- Yeah.

432
00:28:40,008 --> 00:28:41,087
- Get home safe.
- I will.

433
00:28:41,087 --> 00:28:42,453
Bye.

434
00:28:46,372 --> 00:28:49,311
Hey, how long has Ha Na been like this?

435
00:28:49,311 --> 00:28:52,620
Hey. I'm her paid bodyguard.

436
00:28:52,620 --> 00:28:54,354
I can't tell you anything.

437
00:28:54,354 --> 00:28:55,415
You little...

438
00:28:55,415 --> 00:28:57,181
Seriously...

439
00:28:57,941 --> 00:28:59,817
Hey.

440
00:28:59,817 --> 00:29:02,088
Remember?

441
00:29:02,088 --> 00:29:04,019
Back in 11th grade,

442
00:29:04,019 --> 00:29:07,635
the one time I beat you.

443
00:29:07,635 --> 00:29:11,306
<i>I finally beat you.</i>

444
00:29:11,306 --> 00:29:12,983
<i>What?</i>

445
00:29:12,983 --> 00:29:15,101
<i>You lost. What's so funny?</i>

446
00:29:15,101 --> 00:29:17,228
<i>- You're so annoying.
- That's the point.</i>

447
00:29:17,228 --> 00:29:19,507
<i>Why do I feel like I lost?</i>

448
00:29:19,507 --> 00:29:21,566
<i>No. You totally beat me today.</i>

449
00:29:21,566 --> 00:29:23,485
<i>Congrats, Yoon Ha Ru.</i>

450
00:29:23,485 --> 00:29:25,992
<i>- Okay.
- Smile.</i>

451
00:29:25,992 --> 00:29:29,416
<i>One, two, three.</i>

452
00:29:29,416 --> 00:29:31,984
<i>Wait! Let me in!</i>

453
00:29:31,984 --> 00:29:34,454
<i>- Okay, smile.
- Wait!</i>

454
00:29:34,454 --> 00:29:36,357
<i>Hey, come here.</i>

455
00:29:36,357 --> 00:29:38,193
<i>What?</i>

456
00:29:38,193 --> 00:29:40,085
<i>Switch places with me.</i>

457
00:29:40,085 --> 00:29:42,074
<i>Why?</i>

458
00:29:42,074 --> 00:29:44,378
<i>Just shut up and switch.</i>

459
00:29:45,068 --> 00:29:46,591
<i>Oppa.</i>

460
00:29:46,591 --> 00:29:47,952
<i>What? "Oppa?"</i>

461
00:29:47,952 --> 00:29:49,658
<i>Fine, fine.</i>

462
00:29:53,212 --> 00:29:56,389
<i>- Ha Ru, squeeze in.
- Okay.</i>

463
00:29:59,463 --> 00:30:03,247
<i>One, two, three!</i>

464
00:30:10,795 --> 00:30:13,568
Of course I remember.

465
00:30:13,568 --> 00:30:19,534
Do you know what Ha Na
whispered in my ear that day?

466
00:30:21,472 --> 00:30:23,921
What did she say?

467
00:30:23,921 --> 00:30:25,552
Curious?

468
00:30:25,552 --> 00:30:26,928
Yeah.

469
00:30:26,928 --> 00:30:28,348
Come here.

470
00:30:29,876 --> 00:30:31,371
Closer.

471
00:30:33,748 --> 00:30:36,641
It's a secret.

472
00:30:36,641 --> 00:30:38,017
Oh, come on!

473
00:30:38,017 --> 00:30:39,562
I'm not telling you either.

474
00:30:39,562 --> 00:30:44,072
You tell me first if you want to know.

475
00:30:51,302 --> 00:30:53,351
Just...

476
00:30:53,351 --> 00:30:56,324
Don't do this anymore.

477
00:32:00,807 --> 00:32:02,416
[Anonymous Forum]

478
00:32:04,413 --> 00:32:06,110
[The Truth About Yoon Ha Na
Who Fooled the Nation]

479
00:32:07,101 --> 00:32:09,419
I don't want to go.

480
00:32:09,419 --> 00:32:10,835
You want me to leave?

481
00:32:10,835 --> 00:32:12,513
Sun Ah.

482
00:32:12,513 --> 00:32:14,325
Do you really want me to go?

483
00:32:15,610 --> 00:32:17,367
Why won't you stop me?

484
00:32:17,367 --> 00:32:21,201
Why... won't you ever let me in?

485
00:32:37,739 --> 00:32:39,320
That's it.

486
00:32:45,270 --> 00:32:46,706
Cry.

487
00:32:48,164 --> 00:32:49,794
Come on, cry.

488
00:32:51,284 --> 00:32:52,839
Please...

489
00:33:07,512 --> 00:33:08,389
Cut.

490
00:33:08,389 --> 00:33:10,042
Cut!

491
00:33:12,300 --> 00:33:13,713
Sorry, sir.

492
00:33:13,713 --> 00:33:16,967
Maybe I'm dehydrated. Why won't the tears come?

493
00:33:16,967 --> 00:33:19,601
Crying's my specialty.
This shouldn't be happening.

494
00:33:19,601 --> 00:33:20,626
Right?

495
00:33:20,626 --> 00:33:22,866
It's okay. We'll go again.

496
00:33:22,866 --> 00:33:24,314
Let's take a quick break.

497
00:33:24,314 --> 00:33:26,119
- Let's reconvene in ten.
- We'll take ten.

498
00:33:26,119 --> 00:33:28,696
- Okay!
- Ten-minute break!

499
00:33:29,522 --> 00:33:30,985
Is something wrong?

500
00:33:30,985 --> 00:33:34,196
No. I told you. I'm just dehydrated.

501
00:33:34,196 --> 00:33:35,771
If today is too much, tell me.

502
00:33:35,771 --> 00:33:38,448
We can move things around. Whatever you need.

503
00:33:38,448 --> 00:33:40,378
I'm your upperclassman, remember?

504
00:33:40,378 --> 00:33:42,111
Put me to use.

505
00:33:42,111 --> 00:33:44,071
Okay. I will.

506
00:33:44,071 --> 00:33:45,121
Thanks.

507
00:33:45,121 --> 00:33:46,963
Don't worry. Get some rest.

508
00:34:22,948 --> 00:34:25,509
This is so frustrating.

509
00:34:25,509 --> 00:34:28,395
Why can't I cry?

510
00:34:29,082 --> 00:34:31,878
Why is it so hard?

511
00:34:34,740 --> 00:34:36,883
Just drink this first.

512
00:34:44,710 --> 00:34:46,726
It's good.

513
00:34:54,947 --> 00:34:56,936
What do you think it is?

514
00:34:58,426 --> 00:35:00,360
What?

515
00:35:00,360 --> 00:35:02,840
What Sun Ah's feeling.

516
00:35:08,986 --> 00:35:10,613
Regret.

517
00:35:12,599 --> 00:35:13,882
"Regret?"

518
00:35:14,886 --> 00:35:16,349
Yeah.

519
00:35:20,033 --> 00:35:22,410
She doesn't believe in herself.

520
00:35:22,410 --> 00:35:25,380
Jae Hee shines so bright,

521
00:35:25,380 --> 00:35:28,213
she thinks she's not good enough for him.

522
00:35:29,180 --> 00:35:34,091
She loves him so much, but she can't show it.

523
00:35:35,569 --> 00:35:38,109
Jae Hee kept giving her chances.

524
00:35:38,109 --> 00:35:40,109
To come closer.

525
00:35:40,939 --> 00:35:42,809
To hold him.

526
00:35:45,851 --> 00:35:47,555
But still...

527
00:35:48,286 --> 00:35:50,959
Sun Ah let every chance slip away.

528
00:35:52,874 --> 00:35:55,415
She never told him how she felt.

529
00:35:57,045 --> 00:36:01,680
And now she'll never see him again.

530
00:36:01,680 --> 00:36:03,823
She wishes she'd said something...

531
00:36:05,995 --> 00:36:07,995
She regrets it so much.

532
00:36:13,271 --> 00:36:16,794
That's how I think Sun Ah feels.

533
00:36:21,319 --> 00:36:23,419
That's sad.

534
00:36:26,650 --> 00:36:28,487
Ha Na.

535
00:36:28,487 --> 00:36:29,760
You need to go back in.

536
00:36:29,760 --> 00:36:32,150
Let's get your makeup touched up.

537
00:36:42,574 --> 00:36:44,239
Sir.

538
00:36:44,239 --> 00:36:47,207
- Have some coffee.
- Thanks.

539
00:36:48,941 --> 00:36:51,785
What's gotten into Ha Na lately?

540
00:36:51,785 --> 00:36:56,144
It's not just the crying.
There's no emotion in her acting at all.

541
00:36:56,144 --> 00:36:57,881
And she's going to Hollywood like that?

542
00:36:57,881 --> 00:36:59,701
No way.

543
00:37:00,611 --> 00:37:03,321
She's not doing your next project anyway, huh?

544
00:37:03,321 --> 00:37:05,221
That's probably a good thing for us.

545
00:37:05,221 --> 00:37:08,042
How did she fall off so fast?

546
00:37:08,042 --> 00:37:10,897
She might just embarrass herself
in Hollywood...

547
00:37:10,897 --> 00:37:12,662
Seriously...

548
00:37:12,662 --> 00:37:14,256
Hey.

549
00:37:14,985 --> 00:37:16,430
Yes?

550
00:37:16,430 --> 00:37:18,409
Watch what you say.

551
00:37:18,409 --> 00:37:19,926
She's one of our actors.

552
00:37:19,926 --> 00:37:21,793
- Sorry.
- Yeah.

553
00:37:21,793 --> 00:37:23,309
Sir!

554
00:37:24,005 --> 00:37:25,490
This...

555
00:37:26,165 --> 00:37:28,690
- What is it?
- You need to see this.

556
00:37:28,690 --> 00:37:30,146
[Yoon Ha Na Under Fire Over Attitude
and Drug Addiction Allegations]

557
00:37:32,607 --> 00:37:34,591
<i>For what? I already can't stand him.</i>

558
00:37:34,591 --> 00:37:36,060
[Taking pills!]

559
00:37:36,060 --> 00:37:38,855
<i>You know who I am, right?</i>

560
00:37:38,855 --> 00:37:40,594
<i>I'm Yoon Ha Na.</i>

561
00:37:43,678 --> 00:37:45,155
CEO Seo is here.

562
00:37:45,155 --> 00:37:47,655
- Oh, ma'am.
- Ye Rang? When did you get here?

563
00:37:47,655 --> 00:37:49,746
- Get the car ready. Now.
- Sorry?

564
00:37:49,746 --> 00:37:51,910
What are you talking about?
We're still shooting.

565
00:37:51,910 --> 00:37:54,285
- Hurry!
- Yes.

566
00:37:55,117 --> 00:37:57,366
What's going on?

567
00:37:57,366 --> 00:37:59,366
Damn it.

568
00:38:13,848 --> 00:38:15,387
Ha Na.

569
00:38:18,236 --> 00:38:19,520
Stop drinking.

570
00:38:19,520 --> 00:38:22,392
- Let go.
- I said stop!

571
00:38:29,005 --> 00:38:30,487
Take a break.

572
00:38:30,487 --> 00:38:32,239
Ha Na.

573
00:38:32,239 --> 00:38:36,353
Since it's come to this,
take some time off and get treatment.

574
00:38:37,086 --> 00:38:41,637
You want me to make
those damn rumors look true?

575
00:38:41,637 --> 00:38:44,419
You just look like
you're having a really hard time.

576
00:38:46,555 --> 00:38:48,913
I'm perfectly fine.

577
00:38:51,928 --> 00:38:53,626
Ha Na.

578
00:38:54,501 --> 00:38:56,509
You're not fine.

579
00:38:57,142 --> 00:39:00,461
It's okay to let go when you need to.

580
00:39:01,506 --> 00:39:03,371
Like you did?

581
00:39:07,921 --> 00:39:09,051
What?

582
00:39:09,051 --> 00:39:13,948
You mean like when you gave up judo?

583
00:39:15,932 --> 00:39:19,108
- No, I...
- Taking a break?

584
00:39:19,108 --> 00:39:20,673
Sure, sounds great.

585
00:39:20,673 --> 00:39:24,076
But what do you get after running away?

586
00:39:24,076 --> 00:39:26,320
You ended up a bodyguard.

587
00:39:26,320 --> 00:39:28,344
I can't do that.

588
00:39:28,344 --> 00:39:30,357
I'm going to keep acting.

589
00:39:31,751 --> 00:39:33,512
I'm not taking a break.

590
00:40:36,419 --> 00:40:38,579
[Capturing Your Shining Moments]

591
00:41:00,765 --> 00:41:02,371
<i>Ta-da!</i>

592
00:41:02,371 --> 00:41:04,395
<i>Pretty, right?</i>

593
00:41:04,395 --> 00:41:05,807
<i>Yeah.</i>

594
00:41:07,021 --> 00:41:09,780
<i>Come on. It's not the end of the world.</i>

595
00:41:09,780 --> 00:41:13,259
<i>You can't do judo anymore.
So what? Is your life over?</i>

596
00:41:16,163 --> 00:41:17,962
<i>Look at me.</i>

597
00:41:20,285 --> 00:41:24,622
<i>To me, you're still just as amazing.</i>

598
00:41:24,622 --> 00:41:28,421
<i>Judo or no judo, nothing's changed.</i>

599
00:41:31,811 --> 00:41:35,300
<i>I'm not good at anything anymore.</i>

600
00:41:35,300 --> 00:41:37,805
<i>Sure you are.</i>

601
00:41:41,306 --> 00:41:43,506
<i>Protect me.</i>

602
00:41:43,506 --> 00:41:47,437
<i>When I become a famous actress someday,</i>

603
00:41:47,437 --> 00:41:49,388
<i>you can protect me.</i>

604
00:41:50,457 --> 00:41:53,187
<i>You are one of the best
high school judo players in the country.</i>

605
00:41:53,187 --> 00:41:55,451
<i>Who else could protect me?</i>

606
00:41:55,451 --> 00:41:56,997
<i>Right?</i>

607
00:41:56,997 --> 00:41:58,127
<i>Right?</i>

608
00:41:58,127 --> 00:42:00,017
<i>Right?</i>

609
00:42:00,017 --> 00:42:01,314
<i>Right?</i>

610
00:42:01,314 --> 00:42:02,521
<i>Right?</i>

611
00:42:02,521 --> 00:42:05,496
<i>- You smiled! Finally!
- I did not.</i>

612
00:42:05,496 --> 00:42:07,902
<i>You did.</i>

613
00:42:26,976 --> 00:42:28,954
Yoon Ha Na.

614
00:42:30,627 --> 00:42:32,941
You're the worst.

615
00:42:40,149 --> 00:42:42,066
Of course she's attending the awards.

616
00:42:42,066 --> 00:42:44,253
Just think about it.

617
00:42:44,253 --> 00:42:48,652
Do you really think she would act like that
on a plane full of people?

618
00:42:50,264 --> 00:42:52,561
Of course we have evidence to prove otherwise.

619
00:42:52,561 --> 00:42:57,616
If you still choose to believe
such ridiculous rumors, we're done here.

620
00:42:59,548 --> 00:43:01,298
Damn it!

621
00:43:01,298 --> 00:43:04,773
All this over some ridiculous rumor...

622
00:44:13,209 --> 00:44:14,751
Don't be scared.

623
00:44:14,751 --> 00:44:16,694
Just be yourself.

624
00:44:25,116 --> 00:44:27,111
So beautiful!

625
00:45:32,922 --> 00:45:35,624
When they laughed, we laughed with them.

626
00:45:35,624 --> 00:45:39,251
And when they cried,
they moved an entire nation.

627
00:45:39,251 --> 00:45:43,590
Now it's time to honor
the very best in Korean cinema.

628
00:45:43,590 --> 00:45:46,071
Best Actress.

629
00:45:46,071 --> 00:45:50,264
Presenting the award is last year's winner,
actress Lee Hyun Jin.

630
00:45:50,264 --> 00:45:54,918
Last year, Lee Hyun Jin starred in
"Silver Grass" as Hannah,

631
00:45:54,918 --> 00:46:00,479
a woman born and raised in America
who never truly found a place to belong,

632
00:46:00,479 --> 00:46:03,877
capturing an immigrant's loss and longing.

633
00:46:03,877 --> 00:46:09,691
Today, she is an acclaimed actress
whose work transcends borders and languages.

634
00:46:09,691 --> 00:46:11,310
Just leave it there, please.

635
00:46:11,310 --> 00:46:12,403
- Here?
- Thank you.

636
00:46:12,403 --> 00:46:14,093
- Have a good one.
- Thanks.

637
00:46:14,093 --> 00:46:15,893
I'll put these flowers inside.

638
00:46:16,664 --> 00:46:19,153
You can leave them here.
We'll deliver them all together.

639
00:46:19,153 --> 00:46:20,287
Okay.

640
00:46:20,287 --> 00:46:22,251
- These too...
- Just put them down there.

641
00:46:22,251 --> 00:46:23,671
Okay.

642
00:46:28,080 --> 00:46:30,895
Hello, I'm Lee Hyun Jin.

643
00:46:34,170 --> 00:46:36,098
Thank you.

644
00:46:36,098 --> 00:46:41,853
It feels like yesterday
I stood here with my heart pounding.

645
00:46:41,853 --> 00:46:45,516
I can't believe it's already been a year.

646
00:46:45,516 --> 00:46:48,759
<i>It feels strange being back up here.</i>

647
00:46:48,759 --> 00:46:52,948
<i>I can only imagine
how hard you worked behind the scenes,</i>

648
00:46:52,948 --> 00:46:56,809
through all those long, grueling days.

649
00:46:56,809 --> 00:46:58,651
For all the time and passion you poured

650
00:46:58,651 --> 00:47:00,747
- Ha Na.
- into your films...

651
00:47:00,747 --> 00:47:04,793
Whatever anyone says,
you're the best actress in the world to me.

652
00:47:04,793 --> 00:47:06,613
You know that, right?

653
00:47:06,613 --> 00:47:08,349
Of course I do.

654
00:47:08,349 --> 00:47:10,215
Thank you so much.

655
00:47:10,215 --> 00:47:12,846
Now, shall we see who won?

656
00:47:18,101 --> 00:47:22,534
The 30th Baekryong Film Awards, 2026.

657
00:47:22,534 --> 00:47:25,245
And the award for Best Actress goes to...

658
00:47:30,672 --> 00:47:34,531
Yoon Ha Na, from "I Was There in Your Night."

659
00:47:34,531 --> 00:47:36,351
Congratulations.

660
00:47:37,576 --> 00:47:40,746
In director Yang Jun Mo's film
"I Was There in Your Night,"

661
00:47:40,746 --> 00:47:43,021
Yoon Ha Na played Cha Hee,

662
00:47:43,021 --> 00:47:46,588
<i>capturing the finest shades of human emotion</i>

663
00:47:46,588 --> 00:47:49,859
in a performance that deeply moved audiences.

664
00:47:49,859 --> 00:47:55,844
Tonight feels like a fitting tribute
to all her dedication and sincerity.

665
00:47:55,844 --> 00:48:01,311
Now, let's hear from
this year's Best Actress, Yoon Ha Na.

666
00:48:03,681 --> 00:48:05,681
Thank you.

667
00:48:06,816 --> 00:48:10,571
This trophy feels especially heavy tonight.

668
00:48:26,377 --> 00:48:31,610
There's been a lot of talk about me lately.

669
00:48:33,301 --> 00:48:35,301
Those videos...

670
00:48:36,754 --> 00:48:38,014
They're real.

671
00:48:38,014 --> 00:48:42,327
I haven't exactly been myself lately.

672
00:48:43,353 --> 00:48:48,799
I've been having some trouble feeling emotions.

673
00:48:48,799 --> 00:48:51,694
So yes, I've been seeing a doctor.

674
00:48:51,694 --> 00:48:54,687
I'm taking medication and getting treatment.

675
00:48:54,687 --> 00:48:59,343
And yes, that was me
in the video from the plane.

676
00:48:59,343 --> 00:49:02,406
What's going on?

677
00:49:02,406 --> 00:49:03,956
Oh, dear...

678
00:49:03,956 --> 00:49:06,315
My poor girl...

679
00:49:06,315 --> 00:49:07,877
<i>But...</i>

680
00:49:07,877 --> 00:49:12,257
<i>Even if I'm a little broken,
I still know right from wrong.</i>

681
00:49:12,257 --> 00:49:18,453
The only person I've ever told
I can't stand is Yoon Ha Ru.

682
00:49:20,315 --> 00:49:23,560
If I ever said that to someone else
like in that edited clip,

683
00:49:23,560 --> 00:49:27,984
my mom would probably kill me first.

684
00:49:34,143 --> 00:49:38,491
I hope you'll believe me.

685
00:49:38,491 --> 00:49:40,291
And...

686
00:49:42,745 --> 00:49:47,676
I'm going to take
a little time off and come back.

687
00:49:48,372 --> 00:49:50,336
I won't be gone long.

688
00:49:50,336 --> 00:49:53,639
I bounce back pretty fast.

689
00:49:58,344 --> 00:50:00,295
<i>Thank you so much.</i>

690
00:50:07,017 --> 00:50:08,773
My daughter...

691
00:50:08,773 --> 00:50:10,489
You're the bomb.

692
00:50:10,489 --> 00:50:13,151
Two thumbs way up.

693
00:50:13,151 --> 00:50:16,631
Yeah... that was awesome.

694
00:50:19,362 --> 00:50:23,328
Would you stop stuffing your face
at a time like this?

695
00:50:24,256 --> 00:50:26,759
Leave him alone.

696
00:50:26,759 --> 00:50:29,698
- I loved your movie.
- Let's get a picture. One, two!

697
00:50:29,698 --> 00:50:32,300
One more. One, two!

698
00:50:32,300 --> 00:50:33,457
Beautiful.

699
00:50:33,457 --> 00:50:34,862
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

700
00:50:34,862 --> 00:50:35,966
Thank you.

701
00:50:35,966 --> 00:50:37,719
It's such an honor to get a photo with you.

702
00:50:37,719 --> 00:50:40,288
- Thank you.
- Get some rest.

703
00:50:41,166 --> 00:50:43,512
- Congratulations, Ha Na.
- Thank you.

704
00:50:43,512 --> 00:50:44,600
- We'll head over first.
- Okay.

705
00:50:44,600 --> 00:50:46,184
- You looked amazing tonight.
- See you.

706
00:50:46,184 --> 00:50:48,360
- I'll get the car ready.
- Okay.

707
00:50:48,360 --> 00:50:50,855
- Should we get going too?
- Yeah, let's go.

708
00:50:50,855 --> 00:50:53,739
We'll head over first. Take your time.

709
00:50:53,739 --> 00:50:56,650
Ha Na, you were incredible tonight.

710
00:50:56,650 --> 00:50:58,822
- See you later.
- Thanks.

711
00:50:58,822 --> 00:51:00,350
See you soon.

712
00:51:03,049 --> 00:51:04,410
Take care of Ha Na.

713
00:51:04,410 --> 00:51:07,523
- Let's get you changed.
- Yeah.

714
00:51:28,176 --> 00:51:30,403
Everyone's leaving. Let's go.

715
00:51:30,403 --> 00:51:31,872
Yeah.

716
00:51:34,858 --> 00:51:36,858
Hey, Jung Woo Jae.

717
00:51:39,279 --> 00:51:41,176
You know...

718
00:51:42,073 --> 00:51:44,609
about what I said yesterday...

719
00:51:45,485 --> 00:51:47,375
Oh, hold on.

720
00:51:47,375 --> 00:51:48,937
[Seok Min]

721
00:51:50,603 --> 00:51:52,917
<i>Ha Na, we're all ready.</i>

722
00:51:52,917 --> 00:51:55,230
Yeah, I'm coming out now.

723
00:51:56,671 --> 00:51:58,457
Woo Jae.

724
00:51:59,250 --> 00:52:01,509
I mean...

725
00:52:01,509 --> 00:52:03,775
about yesterday...

726
00:52:07,265 --> 00:52:10,091
Why the long face on a night like this?

727
00:52:10,783 --> 00:52:12,687
I'm fine.

728
00:52:12,687 --> 00:52:14,494
Don't worry about me.

729
00:52:18,110 --> 00:52:19,703
Let's go.

730
00:52:20,820 --> 00:52:22,260
Okay.

731
00:52:26,341 --> 00:52:27,576
[Actress Yoon Ha Na]

732
00:53:07,479 --> 00:53:08,662
Woo Jae.

733
00:53:08,662 --> 00:53:10,373
Woo Jae, open the door.

734
00:53:10,373 --> 00:53:12,044
Jung Woo Jae!

735
00:53:30,427 --> 00:53:32,868
Jung Woo Jae!

736
00:53:32,868 --> 00:53:34,212
Jung Woo Jae!

737
00:53:34,212 --> 00:53:36,181
What's wrong? Hey!

738
00:53:37,897 --> 00:53:39,923
Jung Woo Jae!

739
00:53:54,625 --> 00:53:56,451
What are you doing here?

740
00:54:01,949 --> 00:54:04,366
Mr. Jung! Mr. Jung!

741
00:54:13,887 --> 00:54:15,126
Woo Jae...

742
00:54:15,126 --> 00:54:16,925
Jung Woo Jae!

743
00:54:18,062 --> 00:54:19,936
Oh my...

744
00:54:19,936 --> 00:54:22,147
Call an ambulance... Please!

745
00:54:22,147 --> 00:54:23,484
Okay.

746
00:54:23,484 --> 00:54:25,331
- I'll get help.
- Woo Jae.

747
00:54:25,331 --> 00:54:26,810
Stay with me.

748
00:54:26,810 --> 00:54:29,519
- Woo Jae.
- Emergency services?

749
00:54:40,168 --> 00:54:41,806
Ha Na.

750
00:54:59,827 --> 00:55:01,827
Thank goodness...

751
00:55:03,611 --> 00:55:05,032
No.

752
00:55:05,032 --> 00:55:06,442
No.

753
00:55:06,442 --> 00:55:08,264
This can't be...

754
00:55:23,501 --> 00:55:25,126
Woo Jae...

755
00:55:26,461 --> 00:55:28,353
Woo Jae.

756
00:55:28,962 --> 00:55:30,433
No...

757
00:55:30,433 --> 00:55:32,076
This can't be...

758
00:55:32,076 --> 00:55:33,593
Woo Jae.

759
00:55:33,593 --> 00:55:34,966
What do I do...

760
00:55:34,966 --> 00:55:37,496
No, Woo Jae...

761
00:55:37,496 --> 00:55:40,788
No way...

762
00:55:40,788 --> 00:55:44,315
Woo Jae, wake up.

763
00:55:44,315 --> 00:55:46,815
What do I do...

764
00:55:46,815 --> 00:55:49,546
<i>Actress Yoon Ha Na's bodyguard has died.</i>

765
00:55:49,546 --> 00:55:54,573
<i>The suspect reportedly entered the scene
disguised as a flower deliveryman.</i>

766
00:55:54,573 --> 00:56:00,262
<i>Police confirmed that someone
had been stalking Ms. Yoon for some time.</i>

767
00:56:00,262 --> 00:56:05,489
<i>It remains unclear whether
the suspect is the same person.</i>

768
00:56:05,489 --> 00:56:09,883
<i>Police are investigating
the possible connection and circumstances.</i>

769
00:56:09,883 --> 00:56:13,431
<i>Ms. Yoon is reportedly in a state of shock</i>

770
00:56:13,431 --> 00:56:17,570
<i>and has suspended all public appearances.</i>

771
00:56:27,478 --> 00:56:28,696
[Yoon Ha Na]

772
00:56:32,047 --> 00:56:33,274
[When you're feeling anxious]
[Cut back on caffeine and alcohol]

773
00:56:33,274 --> 00:56:34,730
[Only one coffee a day]
[Don't overthink things]

774
00:56:37,607 --> 00:56:39,719
[Ha Na's Medications]
[Precautions]

775
00:56:46,913 --> 00:56:49,087
These are all notes for me.

776
00:57:05,647 --> 00:57:07,240
What's this doing here?

777
00:57:07,240 --> 00:57:08,315
[Yoon Ha Na]

778
00:57:21,860 --> 00:57:23,788
<i>Is this recording?</i>

779
00:57:27,293 --> 00:57:29,835
<i>Hey, Yoon Ha Na.</i>

780
00:57:29,835 --> 00:57:31,516
<i>It's me.</i>

781
00:57:34,008 --> 00:57:37,392
<i>First off, congrats on Best Actress.</i>

782
00:57:41,428 --> 00:57:44,057
<i>The awards are actually tomorrow,</i>

783
00:57:44,057 --> 00:57:48,440
<i>but honestly, I can't see anyone else winning.</i>

784
00:57:48,440 --> 00:57:50,755
<i>So I'm recording this early.</i>

785
00:57:51,776 --> 00:57:57,239
<i>By now, you're probably holding that trophy,
over the moon.</i>

786
00:57:58,952 --> 00:58:00,967
Jung Woo Jae...

787
00:58:00,967 --> 00:58:02,829
<i>I got this camcorder fixed.</i>

788
00:58:02,829 --> 00:58:04,458
<i>Pretty good, right?</i>

789
00:58:05,197 --> 00:58:11,429
All our old videos were still on here.

790
00:58:11,429 --> 00:58:14,429
We really shone back then.

791
00:58:19,553 --> 00:58:21,423
And...

792
00:58:23,175 --> 00:58:26,323
You're still shining just as bright.

793
00:58:27,657 --> 00:58:30,259
So don't worry.

794
00:58:35,702 --> 00:58:38,701
To me, no one shines brighter...

795
00:58:40,314 --> 00:58:42,358
than you.

796
00:58:42,358 --> 00:58:44,172
Yoon Ha Na.

797
00:58:50,032 --> 00:58:52,796
<i>This is kind of embarrassing to say...</i>

798
00:58:52,796 --> 00:58:54,722
Woo Jae...

799
00:58:56,296 --> 00:58:58,507
Jung Woo Jae...

800
00:58:58,507 --> 00:59:02,215
<i>Ha Na, congratulations. I really mean it.</i>

801
01:01:25,260 --> 01:01:27,945
Jung Woo Jae... I miss him.

802
01:01:31,532 --> 01:01:33,798
I miss him so much.

803
01:04:06,943 --> 01:04:08,650
[2010 Haesol City Superintendent's Cup
Judo Tournament]

804
01:04:08,650 --> 01:04:11,277
<i>What is this? Is it a dream?</i>

805
01:04:11,277 --> 01:04:13,741
<i>"2010?"</i>

806
01:04:16,797 --> 01:04:18,580
Everyone in the center, please.

807
01:04:18,580 --> 01:04:21,686
<i>What? Is he talking to me?</i>

808
01:04:21,686 --> 01:04:23,622
Player Yoon Ha Ru, what are you doing?

809
01:04:23,622 --> 01:04:26,102
Come on, onto the mat, please.

810
01:04:26,102 --> 01:04:28,377
<i>Why is he telling me that?</i>

811
01:04:28,377 --> 01:04:31,009
<i>What is this?</i>

812
01:04:35,472 --> 01:04:37,323
<i>Woo Jae?</i>

813
01:04:46,359 --> 01:04:48,346
<i>Jung Woo Jae?</i>

814
01:04:55,230 --> 01:04:57,181
<i>Thank goodness...</i>

815
01:05:07,015 --> 01:05:11,457
<i>To me, no one shines brighter... than you.</i>

816
01:05:11,457 --> 01:05:12,908
<i>Yoon Ha Na.</i>

817
01:05:13,676 --> 01:05:15,374
Woo Jae!

818
01:05:46,826 --> 01:05:47,999
[Epilogue coming up]

819
01:06:03,271 --> 01:06:05,074
<i>Maybe we're still dreaming?</i>

820
01:06:05,074 --> 01:06:07,231
<i>Do you remember anything else?</i>

821
01:06:07,231 --> 01:06:09,670
<i>Where do you think you're touching,
you bastard?</i>

822
01:06:09,670 --> 01:06:13,523
<i>You and I, together, with the camcorder,
fall into a body of water.</i>

823
01:06:13,523 --> 01:06:14,546
<i>Are you okay?</i>

824
01:06:14,546 --> 01:06:16,300
<i>This is crazy!</i>

825
01:06:16,300 --> 01:06:17,469
<i>She's acting...</i>

826
01:06:17,469 --> 01:06:18,462
<i>Totally crazy.</i>

827
01:06:18,462 --> 01:06:19,598
<i>Even weirder than usual.</i>

828
01:06:19,598 --> 01:06:21,361
<i>This is no ordinary training camp.</i>

829
01:06:22,996 --> 01:06:25,197
<i>That place is like the wilderness.</i>

830
01:06:25,197 --> 01:06:28,460
<i>Hide it, he'll dig deeper.
Say you're fine, he'll get suspicious.</i>

831
01:06:28,460 --> 01:06:30,002
<i>What if some small action...</i>

832
01:06:30,002 --> 01:06:33,798
<i>ends up irreversibly changing our past?</i>

833
01:06:33,798 --> 01:06:35,536
<i>What do we do?</i>

834
01:06:35,536 --> 01:06:37,531
<i>We can save him.</i>

835
01:06:39,600 --> 01:06:43,715
[Epilogue]

836
01:06:49,693 --> 01:06:53,086
I could only recover a few of the videos.

837
01:06:56,481 --> 01:06:57,616
It works.

838
01:06:57,616 --> 01:06:59,339
Thank you.

839
01:07:00,609 --> 01:07:02,548
How much do I owe you?

840
01:07:07,491 --> 01:07:10,703
Just give me a thousand won.

841
01:07:11,468 --> 01:07:12,559
Sorry?

842
01:07:12,559 --> 01:07:14,130
But...

843
01:07:14,130 --> 01:07:15,740
It's fine.

844
01:07:16,791 --> 01:07:18,617
Thank you so much.

845
01:07:20,931 --> 01:07:26,554
<i>♪ At my age, after all these years ♪</i>

846
01:07:26,554 --> 01:07:31,636
<i>♪ What sweetness could heartbreak hold? ♪</i>

847
01:07:32,256 --> 01:07:37,066
<i>♪ Still, there's an empty space ♪</i>

848
01:07:37,066 --> 01:07:41,918
<i>♪ Somewhere in my heart ♪</i>

849
01:07:41,918 --> 01:07:47,785
<i>♪ For all that I've lost ♪</i>
